= Work Sharing
    == Maxim Barnstorf
Maxim was responsible for the core implementation of the simulation, from the initial sequential solver through to the final parallel, tiled version, making heavy use of LLMs to assist with the underlying mathematics. The implementation included the main simulation loop, covering the ingestion of the input model files, construction of the absorbing boundary damping profile, and the design and implementation of the tiled update kernels used in the final version. He implemented the MPI domain decomposition and halo exchange, and integrated OpenMP based tiling into the C kernels to reduce memory traffic. He additionally resolved the output bottleneck by parallelizing the compression step and restructuring the HDF5 output so that each rank writes its own file independently.
    == Utkarsh Pathak
Utkarsh developed the additional OpenMP kernel variants v1, v3 and v4 evaluated in the kernel comparison benchmark, and carried out the corresponding performance benchmarking. He contributed to an earlier iteration of the sequential solver, and was responsible for the trace based performance analysis, instrumenting the code with Score-P and producing the resulting Vampir visualizations used to investigate OpenMP barrier behavior and I/O. He also implemented the visualization and plotting of the wavefield output, and refactored the codebase.
